      "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn this section we discuss a generalization of the notion of the\ntangent space introduced in Section <REF_0001>.\nTo do this intelligently, we borrow some notation from\nFormal Deformation Theory, Sections\n<REF_0002>,\n<REF_0003>, and\n<REF_0004>.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be a category fibred in groupoids\nover <MATH_0003>. Given a homomorphism <MATH_0004> of <MATH_0005>-algebras\nand an object <MATH_0006> of <MATH_0007> over <MATH_0008> we write\n<MATH_0009> for the category of lifts of <MATH_0010> to <MATH_0011>.\nAn object of <MATH_0012> is a morphism <MATH_0013> of <MATH_0014>\nlying over <MATH_0015> and morphisms of <MATH_0016>\nare defined as commutative diagrams. The set of isomorphism classes of\n<MATH_0017> is denoted <MATH_0018>. See\nFormal Deformation Theory, Definition <REF_0005> and\nRemark <REF_0006>.\nIf <MATH_0019> is surjective with locally nilpotent kernel we call an element\n<MATH_0020> of <MATH_0021> a <TEXTITOPEN_0001>(infinitesimal) deformation<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> of <MATH_0022>.\nIn this case the <TEXTITOPEN_0002>group of infinitesimal automorphisms of <MATH_0023> over <MATH_0024><TEXTITCLOSE_0002>\nis the kernel\n<MATH_0025>\nNote that an element of <MATH_0026> is the same thing as a lift\nof <MATH_0027> over <MATH_0028> for (the category fibred in sets associated\nto) <MATH_0029>. Compare with\nFormal Deformation Theory, Definition\n<REF_0007> and\nFormal Deformation Theory, Remark\n<REF_0008>.\n\n<STRUCT_0004><STRUCT_0005>\nIf <MATH_0030> is an <MATH_0031>-module we denote <MATH_0032> the <MATH_0033>-algebra whose underlying\n<MATH_0034>-module is <MATH_0035> and whose multiplication is given by\n<MATH_0036>. When <MATH_0037> this is the ring\nof dual numbers over <MATH_0038>, which we denote <MATH_0039> as is customary.\nThere is an <MATH_0040>-algebra map <MATH_0041>. The pullback of <MATH_0042> to <MATH_0043>\nis called the <TEXTITOPEN_0003>trivial deformation<TEXTITCLOSE_0003> of <MATH_0044> to <MATH_0045>.\n\n",
      "source_text_hash": "sha256:e65b745c73058217ee61a36b6aa838fbd7b83b73d638d66c8ab54b19fa4ddbe3",
